# Per-type provenance composition shape for dec:Dispatch (FT-072 / ADR-038).
#
# Per FT-072 §Invariants, Dispatch carries its own mechanical block and
# is never boundary-originated; its shape therefore composes the
# universal mechanical fragment via sh:and but intentionally omits the
# sh:or motivational/boundary alternatives. Dispatch is a structural
# event in the orchestration lifecycle — its "origin" is always the
# orchestrator's own act of placing work on a worker, and that
# attribution is already covered by the mechanical block's
# prov:wasGeneratedBy and prov:wasAttributedTo triples.

@prefix dec:  <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

dec:DispatchProvenanceShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass dec:Dispatch ;
    sh:and ( dec:MechanicalProvenanceShape ) .
